# No line-ending translation, anywhere, ever.
#
# frame/MANIFEST records the SHA-256 of frame/frame_ranked.json,
# frame/candidates.tsv and PREREGISTRATION.md, and PREREGISTRATION.md §10.4
# rests on the claim that "any reader can verify what was written and when,
# independently." Git's autocrlf breaks exactly that: with core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout of frame_ranked.json hashes to 4dcca8bb... while the blob and
# every Linux checkout hash to 4b8be7f2..., so a verifier on another platform
# computes a different digest from the same commit and concludes the record was
# altered.
#
# A hash nobody else can reproduce is not evidence. The repository is therefore
# byte-exact on every platform: working copy == blob == what the manifest signed.
* -text
